{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1364099-help-finding-cod-2e-relevant-information","id":1364099,"title":"Help finding CoD 2e relevant information","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-29T21:53:15-08:00","id":1364099,"title":"Help finding CoD 2e relevant information","content":"I am creating a campaign set in a fantasy victorian/steampunk era. <br /> I have the most of the things on my end done but would love any information I can get. So far the relevant sources I have are the CoD 2e book itself as well as Hurt Locker, and Dark Eras.<br /> Things I am looking for are npc splats, and item statistics at least for now.<br /> Another question is regarding the sample antagonists in the CoD book such as on pg. 119.<br /> For dice pools such as on the Cocky Mob Hitman: Taunting the Mark 4. What does that mean? Is it that I get 4 dice and whatever extra dice that relevant Attributes contribute to doing that roll or do I just roll 4 dice and everything has already been taken into account?<br /> Are there npc splats with out these generalized pools and more traditional stats with specific skills listed on them instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T22:23:59-08:00","id":1364101,"title":"","content":"Characters for which you don't anticipate needing a full stat setup are generally written with dice pools for things they're good at or expected to be able to do; this is also how the &quot;Brief Nightmares&quot; type of Horrors are constructed, with pools for actions the monster is worst at and best at as well as for everything else. The Cocky Mob Hitman rolls four dice to taunt the mark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}